mod-midi-merger (1.0-5~pre3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Depend on mod-host-pistomp (>= 0.10.6-6). The postinst masks the legacy
    image-only systemd units because mod-host loads the merger on demand,
    which is only true from 0.10.6-6: earlier builds resolved no jack >=
    1.9.0 at compile time, so -DHAVE_JACK2 was undefined and
    effects_aggregated_midi_enable was compiled out. Installing this package
    beside an older mod-host would mask the units and leave nothing to load
    the merger, disabling aggregated MIDI mode.

 -- Cam Gorrie <sastraxi@gmail.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 03:53:42 +0000

mod-midi-merger (1.0-5~pre2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild so the event-armed reconcile burst actually ships: the
    1.0-5~pre1 binary was built from the earlier perpetual 2-second poll
    variant of the patch.

 -- Cam Gorrie <sastraxi@gmail.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:37:31 +0000

mod-midi-merger (1.0-5~pre1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Harden hot-plug: NULL guard in the port-registration callback plus an
    event-armed reconcile burst in the merger and broadcaster supervisor.
    A registration wakes the supervisor, which runs a few 1-second reconcile
    scans to connect ports that were not queryable when the callback fired.
    No steady-state polling: the supervisor blocks between events.
  * Mask the legacy image-only systemd units in postinst. mod-host
    loads and unloads the merger on demand via jack_internal_client_load.

 -- Cam Gorrie <sastraxi@gmail.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:29:58 +0000

